WEBVTT

00:24:58.869 --> 00:25:00.250
CM: It's a known problem.

00:25:00.274 --> 00:25:02.615
It's sometimes referred to
as a broken leg problem

00:25:02.639 --> 00:25:05.361
where you're trying to forecast
who's going to win a race,

00:25:05.385 --> 00:25:08.156
and the model doesn't know
that one of the guys is injured.

00:25:08.180 --> 00:25:09.358
There is information,

00:25:09.382 --> 00:25:12.041
when it's sufficiently diagnostic
and outside the model,

00:25:12.065 --> 00:25:14.067
then by all means, override the model.

00:25:14.091 --> 00:25:15.279
You know, it ranges,

00:25:15.303 --> 00:25:17.622
but it's something
like 40 percent of the time,

00:25:17.646 --> 00:25:19.817
the model does better.

00:25:19.841 --> 00:25:21.964
Ten percent of the time
clinical does better,

00:25:21.988 --> 00:25:24.567
and half the time they do about the same.

00:25:24.591 --> 00:25:25.773
AG: All right, well,

00:25:25.797 --> 00:25:28.170
I'm going to hold you
accountable for this, Cade.

00:25:28.194 --> 00:25:29.892
I'm going to send little audio clip

00:25:29.916 --> 00:25:33.464
over to our incoming dean
and our deputy dean,